EXT. FISHING BOAT - DECK - DAWN

Grey sea. Grey sky. A trawler, the SEA WREN, rolling slow. Diesel. Salt.

MAYA TORRES, 16, hoodie soaked, sits on an overturned crate. She holds her phone up. One bar. Flickering.

Her father's boat. Her first trip out. Her last.

LUCAS TORRES, 40s, at the winch, doesn't look at her. He hauls a net. She films him.

MAYA
Say hi to the internet, Dad.

LUCAS
No.

She lowers the phone. Checks it. Notifications stacking.

INSERT - PHONE SCREEN
ON PHONE: jess_wells: where r u
ON PHONE: jess_wells: ur literally everywhere rn
ON PHONE: jess_wells: maya answer

Maya's thumb hovers. Wind. A gull.

MAYA
(typing, murmuring)
Busy.

The phone BUZZES. A call. She takes it.

JESS (V.O.)
(tinny, breathless)
Oh my god, finally. Have you seen it?

MAYA
I'm on a boat, Jess.

JESS (V.O.)
Your video has two million views. Two. Million.

Maya looks at Lucas. He is hauling. He didn't hear.

MAYA
(low)
Which video?

JESS (V.O.)
The one from the dock. Your dad. Yelling at the inspector.

Silence. Maya's stomach drops. She turns her back to him.

MAYA
I deleted that.

JESS (V.O.)
Somebody reposted it. They're calling him the angriest fisherman in America. There's like a hashtag.

Waves. Rope creaking.

LUCAS
(not turning)
Who's on the phone?

MAYA
Nobody.

LUCAS
Maya.

She ends the call. Phone dark. Heart loud.

THE CREW OF THE NEIGHBOURING BOAT lines the rail, forty yards off. Phones raised. They are filming Lucas. They cheer.

THE CREW
(in unison, waving)
Angry Fisherman! Angry Fisherman!

Lucas stops. Turns. Looks at them. Then at her.

Nothing.

LUCAS
(quiet)
How long have you known?

MAYA
Since the dock. I posted it. I was going to take it down.

LUCAS
You posted it.

MAYA
It wasn't supposed to blow up. I just thought, people should see what they do to us.

He wipes his hands on his coat. Slowly. He walks toward her. She stands. He stops an arm's length away.

His face. Unreadable.

Rain begins. Soft, then not.

LUCAS
Give me the phone.

She doesn't.

LUCAS (CONT'D)
Maya. The phone.

She holds it out. He takes it. Looks at the screen. Her face on it. His face on it. Two million.

Wind.

He holds it over the rail.

MAYA
Dad, don't.

LUCAS
(beat)
Show me how to make it say something else.

She stares. Then, shaking, she steps beside him, and takes the phone back.

THE CREW
(distant, still chanting)
Angry Fisherman! Angry Fisherman!

Maya raises the phone. Turns the camera on both of them.
